---
import Product from '../../layouts/Product.astro';
import { products } from '../../data/products';
const product = products.find((p) => p.key === 'render')!;
---
<Product
  product={product}
  heading="Generate documents from your service’s records."
  description="Registry Render produces PDF licences, certificates, letters and receipts from the data your service supplies. Your institution defines the templates and required information; Render checks the inputs and generates the document."
  note="Open-source document generation. Connect it to a new service or one you already run."
>
  <section id="product-example" class="section section-muted" aria-labelledby="render-example-title">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">One example: a professional licence</p>
        <h2 id="render-example-title">Turn the recorded licence details into a document.</h2>
        <p>After the authority has granted a licence, its application supplies the holder’s details and licence terms to Registry Render. Render uses the authority’s template to produce the PDF. The application stores it and makes it available to the licence holder.</p>
      </div>
      <figure class="render-example" aria-labelledby="render-example-caption">
        <section class="source-panel" aria-labelledby="render-source-title">
          <p class="panel-owner">Provided by: your licensing service</p>
          <h3 id="render-source-title">Licence details</h3>
          <dl>
            <div><dt>Holder</dt><dd>Example applicant</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Licence</dt><dd>LIC-2093</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Category</dt><dd>Professional licence</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Valid until</dt><dd>31 October 2029</dd></div>
          </dl>
          <p class="panel-note">The service supplies the data and selects the approved template.</p>
        </section>
        <section class="document-panel" aria-labelledby="render-output-title">
          <p class="panel-owner">Generated by: Registry Render</p>
          <div class="licence-document">
            <p class="document-format">PDF document</p>
            <h3 id="render-output-title">Professional licence</h3>
            <p class="holder-name">Example applicant</p>
            <dl>
              <div><dt>Licence reference</dt><dd>LIC-2093</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Valid until</dt><dd>31 October 2029</dd></div>
            </dl>
          </div>
        </section>
        <figcaption id="render-example-caption">A fictional licence document generated from supplied records and an institution’s template. The licensing service owns the decision and retains the PDF.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="render-capabilities-title">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">Practical capabilities</p>
        <h2 id="render-capabilities-title">Keep the document’s content and layout consistent.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="product-facts">
        <article><h3>Use approved templates</h3><p>Define the layout, labels, fonts and supported languages. Package the reviewed template so the service uses a known version.</p></article>
        <article><h3>Check the required information</h3><p>Set the data each document needs. Render checks the supplied information against that definition before generating the PDF.</p></article>
        <article><h3>Reproduce the same PDF</h3><p>For ordinary PDF rendering, retain the template package, document type, language, data and document timestamp. The same inputs produce the same PDF bytes, so the service can reproduce a document later.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section id="fit" class="section section-muted" aria-labelledby="render-fit-title">
    <div class="section-inner product-fit">
      <div class="section-heading compact">
        <p class="eyebrow">How it fits your service</p>
        <h2 id="render-fit-title">Add document generation beside your records.</h2>
        <p>Use Render from an application, as a local command or embedded in software. It works with the data supplied by the calling service, whether the records are in <a href="/products/base-registry/">Base Registry Engine</a> or another system.</p>
      </div>
      <dl>
        <dt>Your institution defines the document</dt><dd>Agree which information belongs on it, the template and languages, and when the service may issue it.</dd>
        <dt>The application keeps and shares the result</dt><dd>Your implementation stores the PDF and its identifying hashes, then provides the download, printing or document-access route people need.</dd>
        <dt>Choose who runs it</dt><dd>Your institution or appointed provider can host and operate Render, or we can run it for you. We quote hosting and operation separately in the proposal.</dd>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section id="developers" class="section" aria-labelledby="render-developers-title">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <div class="section-heading compact">
        <p class="eyebrow">Evaluate the software</p>
        <h2 id="render-developers-title">Generate your first document.</h2>
        <p>The tutorial generates a local letter and then requests a PDF through the service interface. The <a href="https://docs.registrystack.org/start/registry-render/">Render overview</a> explains the product; the <a href="https://docs.registrystack.org/operate/registry-render/">operations guide</a> covers running it.</p>
        <p><a class="inline-cta" href={product.tutorialHref}>{product.tutorialLabel} →</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Product>

<style>
  .render-example { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1fr); align-items: start; gap: 28px; margin: 0; }
  .source-panel, .document-panel { min-width: 0; border-top: 3px solid var(--registry-blue); padding: 22px; background: var(--registry-white); }
  .panel-owner { margin: 0 0 20px; color: var(--registry-blue); font-size: var(--type-base); font-weight: 600; line-height: 1.5; }
  .source-panel h3 { margin: 0 0 18px; font-size: var(--type-subhead); }
  dl { margin: 0; }
  .render-example dl div { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(95px, 0.8fr) minmax(0, 1.2fr); gap: 12px; padding: 11px 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--registry-rule); }
  .render-example dt { color: var(--registry-muted); font-size: var(--type-md); }
  .render-example dd { margin: 0; font-size: var(--type-md); font-weight: 600; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  .panel-note { color: var(--registry-body); font-size: var(--type-base); line-height: 1.6; margin: 18px 0 0; }
  .licence-document { padding: clamp(20px, 3vw, 32px); border: 1px solid var(--registry-paper-rule); background: var(--registry-paper); }
  .document-format { margin: 0 0 20px; color: var(--registry-blue); font: var(--type-xs)/1.5 var(--registry-mono); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.05em; }
  .licence-document h3 { margin: 0 0 8px; color: var(--registry-blue); font-size: clamp(22px, 2.5vw, 28px); }
  .holder-name { margin: 0 0 24px; font-size: var(--type-lg); }
  .licence-document dl div { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 4px; }
  figcaption { grid-column: 1 / -1; margin: 0; color: var(--registry-muted); font-size: var(--type-base); line-height: 1.6; }
  @media (max-width: 700px) { .render-example { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 20px; } .source-panel, .document-panel { padding: 20px; } }
</style>
